@host = http://localhost:5074

# /dev/seed and /dev/ingest find their files from the repo root (inputs/similarity-sentences.txt, data/corpus).
# Postgres (the default) needs `docker compose up -d`; VectorStore__Provider=inmemory needs nothing but Ollama.
# distance is cosine distance: lower = closer. similarity = 1 - distance, to compare with /similarity.
# Every chunk lives in one collection ("corpus"); chunker= picks one strategy: fixed, heading or lines (the seed).
# /ask searches the heading chunks only (Ask:Chunker) and allows 10 requests per minute per IP (Ask:PermitsPerMinute), then 429.

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### Seed: one chunk per line of inputs/similarity-sentences.txt (10, chunker "lines"). Seeding again replaces the rows.
POST {{host}}/dev/seed

### Ingest data/corpus with both chunkers: per-file and total counts, estimated vs real tokens.
### Again: only changed text is embedded (a second run with no edits: 0 embedded, all unchanged); lost positions are deleted.
POST {{host}}/dev/ingest?chunker=both

### Embed everything again: needed after changing Embedding:Model or Embedding:UseTaskPrefixes (the hash covers the text only)
POST {{host}}/dev/ingest?chunker=both&force=true

### Ingest with one chunker only
POST {{host}}/dev/ingest?chunker=heading

### Read what the heading chunker made of the API docs (in order, with heading path, lines, tokens, hash)
GET {{host}}/dev/chunks?chunker=heading&source=docs/contracts.md

### The same file, fixed windows: look for cut tables and code blocks
GET {{host}}/dev/chunks?chunker=fixed&source=docs/contracts.md

### Step 3.5's five questions, top=3. Run each with chunker=fixed and chunker=heading.
GET {{host}}/search?q=How are internal billing callbacks authenticated?&top=3&chunker=heading

###
GET {{host}}/search?q=Which origins does CORS allow outside Development?&top=3&chunker=heading

###
GET {{host}}/search?q=How is a tenant resolved from a request?&top=3&chunker=heading

###
GET {{host}}/search?q=Is BillingService's queue durable?&top=3&chunker=heading

###
GET {{host}}/search?q=What are the current limitations?&top=3&chunker=heading

### Ask: answered from the docs, with [n] citations (needs POST /dev/ingest first; chat model Chat:*, llama3.2 by default)
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How are internal billing callbacks authenticated?" }

### Ask with top=3
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How is a tenant resolved from a request?", "top": 3 }

### Ask, unrelated: should abstain at the gate (retrieval.gate too_far, usage all null: no model call)
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is the best recipe for banana bread?" }

### Ask, near miss: on topic but not in the docs (verification emails are, the provider isn't); should pass the gate
### and abstain through notInDocs. Not "invoices emailed": that's prompts/ask-v1.md's own example, and llama copies it.
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which email provider sends the verification emails?" }

### Ask, invalid: empty question → 400 invalid_request
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "  " }

### Ask, invalid: top=11 (max 10) → 400 invalid_request
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How is a tenant resolved?", "top": 11 }

### Ask, invalid: top as a string → 400 invalid_request (strict number handling)
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How is a tenant resolved?", "top": "5" }

### The seed sentences only. Monday's prediction: "Caching is enabled." ranks first (negation barely moves an embedding)
GET {{host}}/search?q=Is caching turned off?&chunker=lines

### The tenant sentences and the no-shared-words paraphrase ("No customer can ever see...") should lead
GET {{host}}/search?q=Who can see another tenant's data?&chunker=lines

### The two billing sentences should lead
GET {{host}}/search?q=How are customers billed?&chunker=lines

### Sanity check: an exact copy of a stored sentence, distance about 0 at rank 1
GET {{host}}/search?q=Caching is enabled.&chunker=lines

### Invalid: empty q → 400 invalid_request
GET {{host}}/search?q=

### Invalid: top=0 → 400 invalid_request
GET {{host}}/search?q=caching&top=0

### Invalid: top=50 (max 20) → 400 invalid_request
GET {{host}}/search?q=caching&top=50

### Invalid: unknown chunker → 400 invalid_request, with the names
GET {{host}}/search?q=caching&chunker=headings

### Invalid: lines is the seed's, not a markdown chunker → 400 invalid_request
POST {{host}}/dev/ingest?chunker=lines
